ces, ","type":"text"},{"code":"edges","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is in index order: the ","type":"text"},{"code":"k","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"th position of ","type":"text"},{"code":"edges","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" has ","type":"text"},{"code":"edgeIndex","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"k","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". So an algorithm that gathers edges from the index-space rows can order them by position","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(a tie rule) without walking ","type":"text"},{"code":"edges","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Defaults."}]},{"type":"text","text":" As for "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":", members with default implementations are requirements,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"so a representation’s faster version is the one generic code calls, and a wrapper must forward"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every one."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The protocol has no mutation; mutation belongs to concrete types. It does not refine"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sendable"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/UndirectedView"],"type":"conformingTypes","title":"Conforming Types"}],"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An undirected graph: a finite set of vertices and a finite collection of undirected edges"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"between them. Kept apart from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":": an undirected graph is not a symmetric directed"},{"type":"text","